    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d811">

                <pb facs="1105" n="969" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg969"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.1515/971: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Summerlin</hi>)<anchor n="42" xml:id="d811-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-12T17:00:00-05:00">November 12, 1929—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>82. Legation’s 107, November 7, 4 p.m. The Department desires to fix a date for
                    the convening of the boundary conference which will be most convenient to the
                    Governments of Honduras and Guatemala. Please ascertain and report by telegraph
                    the approximate time when Honduras will be prepared to be represented at the
                    conference. A similar telegram is being addressed to the Legation at
                    Guatemala.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d811-f1" n="42" type="source" xml:id="d811-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, to the Chargé in
                    Guatemala as telegram No. 69, referring to Legation’s telegram No. 133, October
                    28, 7 p.m.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
